# Revenue Dashboard (Excel)

An interactive Excel sales dashboard analyzing global retail sales data, built with PivotTables, PivotCharts, and slicers for dynamic, drill-down analysis.

## Project Overview

This project works with a large raw sales dataset (60,000+ transaction records) and turns it into an interactive, decision-ready revenue dashboard.

**Raw data fields:** Region, SubRegion, Market, Customer, Business Segment, Category, Model, Color, Sales Date, Sales Period, List Price, Unit Price, Order Quantity, Sales Amount.

## What the Dashboard Shows

- **Revenue Share by Region** — pie chart breakdown of sales across global regions
- **Revenue Trend by Month & Year** — line chart tracking performance over time
- **Revenue by Year** — bar chart comparing yearly totals
- **Revenue by Market** — column chart comparing performance across markets
- **Interactive Dashboard** — a combined dashboard sheet with slicers, allowing real-time filtering by category and other dimensions

## Tools & Skills Used

- Microsoft Excel — PivotTables and PivotCharts
- Slicers for interactive, real-time filtering
- Large dataset handling (60,000+ rows)
- Data visualization: pie charts, line charts, bar/column charts
- Dashboard design for business decision-making

## Files

- `Revenue_Dashboard.xlsx` — full interactive workbook (Raw Data + 4 chart sheets + combined Dashboard)

## How to Use

1. Open the file in Microsoft Excel (slicers require Excel 2010+).
2. Go to the **Dashboard** sheet for the combined interactive view.
3. Use the slicers to filter by category, region, or market and watch all charts update in real time.

